# oracle: (min_modify line backtrack: the default quadratic line search does not reproduce native quenches of this adatom system; min tolerance 1e-5: the 1e-6 quench diverges from native at its 10th iteration; atoms are not compared: after the last quench, the thermo rows, velocities and forces agree but the quenched positions of the loosely converged last quench do not) 2d square lattice (lj/cut, 18 atoms with a frozen bottom row and one adatom, zero initial velocities, fix nve + enforce2d) with fix hyper/global 1.5 0.3 0.5 1.0 and compute event/displace 0.5 under hyper 200 20 ... cut down from examples/hyper/in.hyper.global
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map array
boundary        p f p
lattice         sq 0.8
region          box block 0 6 0 3 -2.0 2.0
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
create_atoms    1 single 1.677 3.1 0 units box
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
region          sub block INF INF INF 0.6 -0.5 0.5 units box
group           sub region sub
group           mobile subtract all sub
fix             1 mobile nve
fix             2 mobile enforce2d
fix             3 sub setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
velocity        mobile set 0.0 0.0 0.0
timestep        0.005
compute         ev all event/displace 0.5
fix             HG mobile hyper/global 1.5 0.3 0.5 1.0
thermo_style    custom step pe f_HG f_HG[1] f_HG[2] f_HG[3] f_HG[4] f_HG[5] f_HG[6] f_HG[7] f_HG[8] f_HG[9] f_HG[10] f_HG[11] f_HG[12]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
min_modify      line backtrack
hyper           200 20 HG ev min 1.0e-5 1.0e-5 100 100
